@copilot Simplify the new metric assertions in this PR only. In SpymemcachedTest.storeRejectedAsTooLarge, the corresponding span already checks the version-dependent errorType, and assertDurationMetric already checks the metric's identity/type/unit and exact keys including ERROR_TYPE. Remove the second waitAndAssertMetrics block that repeats ERROR_TYPE and adds a generic hasCount(1). Keep assertDurationMetric and the span and application-outcome assertions unchanged.

Apply the metric-testing guidance proposed in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20738: when corresponding spans already verify attribute values, keep metric identity, type, unit, and exact point attribute-key checks instead of repeating those values. Assert different success/failure point key sets separately, including whether ERROR_TYPE is present. Reuse existing domain helpers or containsOnlyKeys. Keep numeric/value assertions that verify aggregation, duplicate recording, terminal timing, or other metric-specific behavior; this is not a blanket numeric-assertion removal.

Update this existing PR directly on its current head branch. Limit this assignment to the test cleanup described above; do not change production behavior, weaken span assertions, update unrelated PR branches, merge or rebase the stack, or create a duplicate/follow-up PR as a workaround. Preserve the PR's existing base and draft/ready state. Follow repository instructions, apply the narrowest spotlessApply before relevant targeted validation, and keep only meaningful test changes. Acceptance: the identified redundant value assertions are removed, exact metric key-set and metric identity/type/unit coverage remains, and all metric-specific behavior coverage is preserved. Do not post replies to human comments or resolve review threads.

